# Policy Source

This source introduces the mental model of "Policy" as a conceptual tool for navigating complex situations through pattern and relationship recognition. It references Ray Dalio's economic framework where policy operates at the level of systemic rules and incentive structures.
## Cross-Source Perspectives
- Ray Dalio's [[How the Economic Machine Works - Ray Dalio]] frames policy as a macro-level force governing monetary and fiscal systems rather than individual decision heuristics.
## Key Takeaway
Policy functions as a universal mental model applicable across domains, providing a mental shortcut for understanding patterns and relationships in complex situations.
## Confidence
0.7 — moderately established; definition is generic and needs sharper differentiation from adjacent models.